From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 23:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] AML: connect passthrough resume picture hold

Opt the built-in AML renderer into Kodi's generic resume preparation.
Keep the displayed picture across decoder reset, reject stale buffer
generations and release the retained target only through scheduled output.
A successful first QBUF acknowledges submission; scheduling alone does not.

Reset CoreELEC's extra passthrough acquisition observations at preparation
boundaries so they cannot reuse a pre-anchor error. The generic capability
and player phase live in the separate Kodi patch; no addon is required.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/AudioSinkAE.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/AudioSinkAE.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/AudioSinkAE.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/AudioSinkAE.cpp
@@ -417,5 +417,13 @@
   std::unique_lock lock(m_critSection);
   m_syncError = 0.0;
+  m_syncErrorRaw = 0.0;
+  m_syncErrorRawValid = false;
+  m_syncErrorScale = 1.0;
+  m_syncErrorSaturated = false;
+  m_syncErrorAcquire = false;
+  m_syncWasInSync = false;
   m_syncErrorTime = 0;
+  m_syncObservation = {};
+  m_acceptedSyncObservation = {};
   if (m_pAudioStream)
   {
@@ -423,4 +431,5 @@
     // Do not consume a preparation window as a new post-release correction.
     m_syncErrorTime = info.errortime;
+    m_syncWasInSync = info.state == CAESyncInfo::SYNC_INSYNC;
   }
 }
